invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_init leaves the key's second cpu byte as its
  storage held it, so a key that no call gave a description of the CPU
  reads CH_CPU_AVX512 from whatever the stack held. bin/aes_runtime_test
  fills the key with 0xff before the call and requires the byte to read 0
  after it.

--- old
    k->key.cpu = 0;
    k->key.cpu_high = 0;
--- new
    k->key.cpu = 0;
